# NESITE CDN — environment variables
#
# There are NONE required.
#
# Every provider integrated here (Kappa, SenaVuck, SILENTPHANTOM, CMNTY CDN,
# Violetics CDN, Zass CDN, Nekohime Cloud, Catbox) was verified to accept
# anonymous uploads with no key, account, cookie, session or CAPTCHA. The UI
# only ever shows the "No API Key" badge for providers whose audit confirmed
# `requiresAuth: false`.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` only if you add a provider that needs a
# credential.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you ever add an authenticated provider:
#
#   1. Set the secret in Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
#   2. Read it ONLY inside a server route / server action.
#   3. NEVER prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — those are inlined into the client
#      bundle and are readable by anyone who opens devtools.
#
# Example (server-side only):
#
#   SOME_PROVIDER_API_KEY=replace-me
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Hard cap on the body the relay will accept, in bytes. Vercel limits serverless
# request bodies to 4.5 MB, so this must stay below that. It is shared by the
# browser client and the relay so the two can never disagree.
#
# Override only if you deploy somewhere without Vercel's body limit; the UI will
# follow whatever value you set.
#
# NESITE_PROXY_BODY_LIMIT_BYTES=4194304